INT. HOT-AIR BALLOON BASKET - DAWN

A wicker basket rising slowly over a patchwork of fog and green hills. A propane burner roars, then hushes.

SOLOMON ABARA-KITT (30s, sunburned, nervous hands) holds a small velvet box behind his back. ROSALIND "ROZ" PETROV (30s, wind-whipped hair, an easy grin) leans over the edge, taking photos with her phone.

ROZ
Look at that. You can see the whole valley.

SOLOMON
I can see it.

ROZ
You're not looking.

SOLOMON
I'm looking at you.

She turns. Sees his face. Sees the way his hand is behind him.

ROZ
Sol. What's in your hand?

SOLOMON
Nothing.

ROZ
Sol.

SOLOMON
It's a, um. It's a sandwich.

ROZ
It is not a sandwich.

He brings out the box. Opens it. A ring catches the first sun.

SOLOMON
Roz. Will you...

A voice from above them, cheerful, heavily accented.

PILOT (O.S.)
Good morning, lovebirds!

Solomon freezes. Roz looks up. At the top of the basket's rigging, clinging to a rope with one hand and holding a thermos with the other, hangs the PILOT, GUNNAR ECKHARDT (60s, wild white beard, goggles pushed up on a leather cap).

GUNNAR
Do not mind me. I am only checking the knots.

SOLOMON
(through his teeth)
Gunnar. Please.

GUNNAR
Yes, yes, I am very quiet.

He climbs down out of sight. Roz laughs until she cries. Solomon, mortified, looks at the ring.

ROZ
Ask me again.

SOLOMON
Roz Petrov. Will you marry me?

ROZ
Yes.

From somewhere above, faintly:

GUNNAR (O.S.)
Congratulations!
